  "description": "<h3>1960 version: meets a US general in the mountains and founds the Danube Liberation Movement</h3><p>Dimitrov's 1960 account to Sheridan: 'In 1943, the US and the UK sent a military mission to the Balkans under a US general who saw Dimitroff's pamphlets'; the general asked him to lead an underground; he 'formed the Danube Liberation Movement', was seized by the Germans and spared by governor Dimiter Raichev, then escaped to revive it as the Bulgarian Democratic Bloc. None of this appears in the 1950 self-account.</p><table><tr><th align=left valign=top>Event</th><td>6 · underground</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Date</th><td>1943 · quality: claimed</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Place</th><td>Macedonia (region) · role: at</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Fix</th><td>41.3000, 22.3000 · MANUAL (manual)</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Basis</th><td>self_account</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Link note</th><td>'in the Macedonian Mountains'</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Place note</th><td>Fixed manually (see geocode_fixups.sh). The historical region across Greece, North Macedonia and Bulgaria; the file uses it loosely. 'Macedonian Mountains' (p137) attached here.</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Event note</th><td>The 1958 press profile has 'Danube Valley Organization for Resistance' as his first unit, replaced by the Bloc '1944-1953' (p147).</td></tr></table><p><b>Sources</b></p><ul><li>p137 <i>self_account</i> (1960-06-28): “On the basis of this meeting, Dimitroff formed the Danube Liberation Movement”</li><li>p138 <i>self_account</i> (1960-06-28): “escape if possible to the mountains ... to revive his Movement as the Bulgarian Democratic Bloc”</li><li>p147 <i>self_account</i> (1958-04-10): “His first anti-Red unit was the Danube Valley Organization for Resistance”</li></ul>",
