 {
  "id": "stop-10-1-37",
  "name": "1944 · Vardar Macedonia",
  "availability": "1944-01-01T00:00:00Z/1945-12-31T23:59:59Z",
  "description": "<h3>Organizes Agrarian sympathizers in Vardar Macedonia; 1960 version puts him in the mountains with partisans and in contact with Colonel Bakeless and General Crane</h3><p>1950 telling: village-to-village organizing 'upon the advice of a certain General Kitchharov'. 1960 telling: remnants of his group retreat north; he goes to Col. Bakeless of the new US mission; Washington sends no aid; he meets 'General Cook' in Yugoslavia.</p><table><tr><th align=left valign=top>Event</th><td>10 · underground</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Date</th><td>1944 → 1945 · quality: claimed</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Place</th><td>Vardar Macedonia (region, now North Macedonia) · role: at</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Fix</th><td>41.6086, 21.7453 · APPROXIMATE (google)</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Basis</th><td>summary, self_account</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Names in use</th><td>Boris Stoikov</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Place note</th><td>The Yugoslav (now North Macedonian) part of Macedonia.</td></tr></table><p><b>Sources</b></p><ul><li>p37 <i>summary</i> (1969-08-25): “During the war he worked illegally in Greek Macedonia and Vardar, Macedonia to escape the German authorities”</li><li>p67 <i>self_account</i> (1950-10-13): “Allegedly he worked in Vardar Macedonia in order to organize Bulgarian sympathizers for the cause of Dr. G. M. Dimitrov, and upon the advice of a certain General Kitchharov”</li><li>p138 <i>self_account</i> (1960-06-28): “Dimitroff came down to see Colonel Bakless (sic) of the new US military mission to Bulgaria, chief of which was General Crane (sic)”</li></ul>",
