 {
  "id": "stop-12-1-4",
  "name": "1945 · Yugoslavia",
  "availability": "1945-01-01T00:00:00Z/1945-12-31T23:59:59Z",
  "description": "<h3>Travels south-west Yugoslavia on a forged identity card as 'Boris Stoikov'; captured by the Yugoslavs</h3><p>1960 version: seized by Tito's police 'on the way to say goodbye to the General', jailed 65 days on bread and marmalade, interrogated on his US contacts (p138).</p><table><tr><th align=left valign=top>Event</th><td>12 · underground</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Date</th><td>1945 · quality: stated</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Place</th><td>Yugoslavia (country, now former Yugoslavia (Serbia, Croatia, Bosnia, Slovenia, North Macedonia, Montenegro, Kosovo)) · role: at</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Fix</th><td>43.9159, 17.6791 · APPROXIMATE (google)</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Basis</th><td>self_account</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Names in use</th><td>Boris Stoikov</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Place note</th><td>Historical state; Google has no result for 'Yugoslavia', so the Bosnia centroid stands in for the former federation's centre.</td></tr></table><p><b>Sources</b></p><ul><li>p30 <i>self_account</i>: “obtained illegal identity card in name of Boris STOIKOV, a member of the 2nd Belgrade Shock Brigade. Toured south-western Yugoslavia ... Captured by Yugoslav”</li><li>p62 <i>self_account</i> (1950-11-13): “under the name \"Boris Stoikov, a member of the 2nd Belgrade Shock Brigade\", he toured southwestern Yugoslavia”</li><li>p138 <i>self_account</i> (1960-06-28): “Dimitroff was seized by Tito's police and put in jail for 65 days on bread and marmalade”</li></ul>",
