 {
  "id": "stop-13-1-43",
  "name": "1945 · Sofia",
  "availability": "1945-01-01T00:00:00Z/1945-12-31T23:59:59Z",
  "description": "<h3>Sent back toward Bulgaria, escapes in transit, reaches Sofia; sheltered by Belgashki, Col. Bakeless, 'Bucky', General Crane and Minnie Balabanova</h3><p>1953 version: met General Crane in Sofia in 1945, who asked for a program of his organization and took him on (p98). 1960 version: the Yugoslavs handed him to a Bulgarian lieutenant colonel whom he persuaded to defect; both went to Bakeless' house; he then opened an underground HQ 'in a convent about two miles from Sofia' (p138).</p><table><tr><th align=left valign=top>Event</th><td>13 · escape</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Date</th><td>1945 · quality: stated</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Place</th><td>Sofia (city) · role: at</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Fix</th><td>42.6977, 23.3219 · APPROXIMATE (google)</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Basis</th><td>self_account</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Names in use</th><td>Boris Stoikov</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Event note</th><td>The American helpers are named only by Dimitrov.</td></tr></table><p><b>Sources</b></p><ul><li>p30 <i>self_account</i>: “Sent back to Bulgaria; escaped during transfer; reached Sofia where he was helped by Peter BELGASHKI, Colonel BAKELESS, an American sergeant named \"Bucky\", General Craig, and Mrs. Minnie BALABANOVA”</li><li>p98 <i>self_account</i> (1953-07-21): “in 1945 he met the American General Crane in Sofia and the General requested KELLY to prepare a program of his organization”</li><li>p138 <i>self_account</i> (1960-06-28): “they both went to Colonel Bakless' house, where Dimitroff remained to recover his health”</li></ul>",
  "position": {
   "cartographicDegrees": [
    23.3218675,
