 {
  "id": "stop-16-1-43",
  "name": "1946-08-16 · Sofia",
  "availability": "1946-08-16T00:00:00Z/1946-08-16T23:59:59Z",
  "description": "<h3>Captured by police in Sofia; 18 days without bread, 12 without water, 4 days on an 'electric torture machine'</h3><p>Kept alive, he believes, as a prospective witness against Nikola Petkov. 1960 version: betrayed by his landlady for a million leva, questioned by a Soviet commissar, waited nine months for hanging (p139).</p><table><tr><th align=left valign=top>Event</th><td>16 · arrest</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Date</th><td>1946-08-16 · quality: conflicting</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Place</th><td>Sofia (city) · role: at</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Fix</th><td>42.6977, 23.3219 · APPROXIMATE (google)</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Basis</th><td>summary, self_account</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Other dates</th><td>p5 says 1946-10; p107 says 1946-10; p117 says 1946-10; p147 says 1946</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Event note</th><td>The CIA summaries (p117, p5, p107) say October 1946; the 1950 self-account says 16 August 1946. The 1953 version says he was tortured 'approximately six months near Vratsa' (p98).</td></tr></table><p><b>Sources</b></p><ul><li>p5 <i>summary</i>: “October 1946: DIMITROV arrested by the police”</li><li>p30 <i>self_account</i>: “16 August 1946: Captured by police in Sofia. 18 days without bread; 12 days without water. 4 days on an electric torture machine”</li><li>p67 <i>self_account</i> (1950-10-13): “On August 16, 1946, he was captured by the police in Sofia”</li><li>p107 <i>summary</i> (1952-02-29): “In October 1946 he was arrested by the police, sentenced to death”</li><li>p117 <i>summary</i> (1951-05-09): “In October, 1946, he was arrested by the police”</li><li>p139 <i>self_account</i> (1960-06-28): “Dimitroff was betrayed at his [safe] house in Sofia by the landlady for one million leva, and was arrested by the Bulgarian secret police”</li><li>p147 <i>self_account</i> (1958-04-10): “imprisoned and sentenced to death in 1946 after betrayal, tortured by electricity”</li></ul>",
  "position": {
