  "description": "<h3>Crosses the Greek frontier south of Zlatograd</h3><p>The one pre-1950 date the CIA summaries repeat without variation.</p><table><tr><th align=left valign=top>Event</th><td>21 · flight</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Date</th><td>1947-07-23 · quality: stated</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Place</th><td>Greek-Bulgarian frontier south of Zlatograd (frontier) · in the file: “Zlatograd / Rhodope frontier” · role: at</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Fix</th><td>41.3656, 25.0498 · GEOMETRIC_CENTER (google)</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Basis</th><td>summary, self_account</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Names in use</th><td>Diko</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Place note</th><td>The 23 July 1947 crossing point. Web lookup 2026-09-23: the only road crossing here (Zlatograd-Thermes) opened in 2010 on the pass south of the town; used as the nearest modern fix for a mountain crossing. Precision: approximate.</td></tr></table><p><b>Sources</b></p><ul><li>p6 <i>summary</i>: “23 July 1947: He escaped to Greece”</li><li>p31 <i>self_account</i>: “23 July 1947: crossed Greek frontier south of Zlatograd”</li><li>p57 <i>summary</i> (1964-01-20): “He escaped to Greece in 1947”</li><li>p68 <i>self_account</i> (1950-10-13): “On July 23, 1947 he crossed the Greek frontier south of Zlatograd”</li><li>p99 <i>self_account</i> (1953-07-21): “He was assisted by one Fancha Fernandova near Plovdiv. On crossing the Bulgarian border into Greece KELLY stated that he surrendered to a Greek patrol”</li><li>p117 <i>summary</i> (1951-05-09): “On 23 July 1947 he escaped to Greece”</li></ul>",
