 {
  "id": "stop-22-1-79",
  "name": "1947-07-24 · Echinos",
  "availability": "1947-07-24T00:00:00Z/1947-07-24T23:59:59Z",
  "description": "<h3>Gives himself up at Shahim; interrogation centre; approached by British intelligence (Andros, Scott) and the Greek service, refuses both</h3><p>1960 version: UK 'General Scott' offered him 'complete support and a radio station at Salonika'; he refused because Scott 'was very anti-US' (p139).</p><table><tr><th align=left valign=top>Event</th><td>22 · arrest</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Date</th><td>1947-07-24 · quality: stated</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Place</th><td>Echinos (village) · in the file: “Shahim (Echinos?), Greek Thrace” · role: at</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Fix</th><td>41.2754, 24.9723 · APPROXIMATE (google)</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Basis</th><td>self_account</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Names in use</th><td>Diko</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Place note</th><td>The file's 'Shahim': Turkish/Pomak name Şahin of Echinos, a Pomak village north of Xanthi near the Bulgarian border (web lookup 2026-09-23). Where he gave himself up, 24 Jul 1947.</td></tr></table><p><b>Sources</b></p><ul><li>p31 <i>self_account</i>: “24 July 1947: gave himself up at Shahim”</li><li>p99 <i>self_account</i> (1953-07-21): “he was approached by British Intelligence, a Mr. Andros (possibly Andrews) and Mr. Scott ... KELLY also said that the Greek IS had asked him to work for them, and that he refused them also”</li><li>p139 <i>self_account</i> (1960-06-28): “UK General Scott met and offered him complete support and a radio station at Salonika”</li></ul>",
