  "name": "1948 · Athens (from)",
  "availability": "1948-01-01T00:00:00Z/1948-01-02T00:00:00Z",
  "description": "<h3>1960 version: Communist assassins sent to Athens; goes to Italy at Greek suggestion; at Bari in 1949 'Mr. Clark' of the US Embassy brings him back to Greece</h3><p>Only in the 1960 account. The IRO trip to Italy with Flora in 1949 (below) is the likely kernel.</p><table><tr><th align=left valign=top>Event</th><td>26 · flight</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Date</th><td>1948 → 1949 · quality: claimed</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Place</th><td>Athens (city) · role: from</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Fix</th><td>37.9838, 23.7275 · APPROXIMATE (google)</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Basis</th><td>self_account</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Names in use</th><td>Diko; Ulysse 62</td></tr></table><p><b>Sources</b></p><ul><li>p139 <i>self_account</i> (1960-06-28): “During 1948, Communist agents were sent to Athens to kill him. For this reason he went to Italy at the suggestion of the Greek Government. In 1949 while at Bari, a Mr. Clark from the US Embassy in Greece, who knew him as…”</li></ul>",
