 {
  "id": "stop-25-1-65",
  "name": "1948-06 · Athens",
  "availability": "1948-06-01T00:00:00Z/1950-10-31T23:59:59Z",
  "description": "<h3>Broadcasts in Bulgarian on Radio Athens every Sunday evening</h3><p>30,000 drachmae per broadcast, most of it eaten by translation costs for the Greek censor; the Greek government also gave him a room at a run-down New Phaleron hotel and 2,800 drachmae a day (p68-69). This is the 'occasional propaganda for Greeks under nom de plume Diko' of the later summaries (p65, p128).</p><table><tr><th align=left valign=top>Event</th><td>25 · employment</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Date</th><td>1948-06 → 1950-10 · quality: circa</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Place</th><td>Athens (city) · role: at</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Fix</th><td>37.9838, 23.7275 · APPROXIMATE (google)</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Basis</th><td>document, self_account</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Names in use</th><td>Diko; Lyle O. Kelly; Ulysse 62</td></tr></table><p><b>Sources</b></p><ul><li>p31 <i>self_account</i>: “c. June 1948: Athens where he obtained employment broadcasting in Bulgarian on Radio Athens”</li><li>p62 <i>document</i> (1950-11-13): “He now works for Radio Athens and lives at Hotel New Phaleron”</li><li>p68 <i>document</i> (1950-10-13): “He broadcasts every Sunday evening in Bulgarian. He receives 30,000 drachmae per broadcast”</li><li>p84 <i>document</i> (1951-04-18): “he was observed by our people to be going into the Aliens Directorate, Radio Athens, and other official Greek residences”</li></ul>",
  "position": {
