 {
  "id": "stop-27-1-65",
  "name": "1949-02 · Athens",
  "availability": "1949-02-01T00:00:00Z/1949-11-30T23:59:59Z",
  "description": "<h3>Marries Flora Vavanou (Feb 1949), leaves for Italy through IRO in March, returns to Athens in October; daughter born November 1949</h3><p>A marriage of convenience aimed at US visas via Flora's aunt 'Teresa' in Chicago; the pregnancy stopped the emigration (p99). The 1969 dispatch repeats the story with Rome as the place (p39).</p><table><tr><th align=left valign=top>Event</th><td>27 · marriage</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Date</th><td>1949-02 → 1949-11 · quality: stated</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Place</th><td>Athens (city) · role: at</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Fix</th><td>37.9838, 23.7275 · APPROXIMATE (google)</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Basis</th><td>self_account</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Names in use</th><td>Diko</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Event note</th><td>seed_relations gives the marriage as '1949' (c.1949-50); the 1953 account is the only source for February.</td></tr></table><p><b>Sources</b></p><ul><li>p38 <i>self_account</i> (1969-08-25): “KELLY confided that his marriage was recognized by both parties as one of convenience”</li><li>p39 <i>self_account</i> (1969-08-25): “their well laid plans were wrecked by the arrival of a baby daughter while they were in Rome, Italy on their first step toward immigration”</li><li>p99 <i>self_account</i> (1953-07-21): “He married Flora in February 1949 and by the latter part of March they were en route to Italy ... They returned to Athens in October 1949. A daughter was born in November 1949”</li></ul>",
  "position": {
   "cartographicDegrees": [
