 {
  "id": "stop-28-1-65",
  "name": "1949-04-06 · Athens",
  "availability": "1949-04-06T00:00:00Z/1949-04-10T23:59:59Z",
  "description": "<h3>Agent 'Ulysse 62' of the French Ulysse network: two reports in its 1949 files (military situation; Greek Government Council of Coordination)</h3><p>Known from 'a penetration of French intelligence files' (p32). The file also has him in contact with the Barev brothers and the Aliens Directorate, and receiving 'an order from the Americans requesting him to go to Washington for a time' (p106). Nasmith learned 'from Ogive that, in 1949, Kelly worked for Florimond' (p83).</p><table><tr><th align=left valign=top>Event</th><td>28 · contact</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Date</th><td>1949-04-06 → 1949-04-10 · quality: stated</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Place</th><td>Athens (city) · role: at</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Fix</th><td>37.9838, 23.7275 · APPROXIMATE (google)</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Basis</th><td>document, summary</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Names in use</th><td>Diko</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Event note</th><td>Which 1949 dates: p32 gives 6 April twice; p106 gives 10 April and 6 April.</td></tr></table><p><b>Sources</b></p><ul><li>p31 <i>summary</i>: “1949*: worked for Pierre FLORIMOND (French vice consul), Salonika”</li><li>p32 <i>document</i>: “The 1949 files of the French intelligence network \"Ulysse\" ... listed Dimitri DIMITROV as an agent (Ulysse 62)”</li><li>p83 <i>document</i> (1951-04-18): “We have learned from Ogive that, in 1949, Kelly worked for Florimond”</li><li>p104 <i>summary</i> (1953-03-27): “as early as 1949 Subject had been an agent of a French Intelligence network run by the Military Attache of the French Embassy in Athens”</li><li>p106 <i>document</i> (1952-04-04): “the 1949 files of French Intelligence network \"Ulysse\" of Captain Michel de la Roncier ... listed Dimitri Dimitrov as an agent”</li></ul>",
  "position": {
   "cartographicDegrees": [
