  "description": "<h3>Works for the Propaganda Section of the Greek General Staff after returning to Athens; writes anti-Communist books with a Greek translator</h3><table><tr><th align=left valign=top>Event</th><td>29 · employment</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Date</th><td>1949-10 → 1950 · quality: stated</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Place</th><td>Athens (city) · role: at</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Fix</th><td>37.9838, 23.7275 · APPROXIMATE (google)</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Basis</th><td>document, self_account</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Names in use</th><td>Diko; Lyle O. Kelly</td></tr></table><p><b>Sources</b></p><ul><li>p69 <i>document</i> (1950-10-13): “Part 7 (enclosure No. 3) is being published by the Greek General Staff and is at the printers at the present time”</li><li>p100 <i>self_account</i> (1953-07-21): “KELLY worked for the Propaganda Section of the Greek General Staff headed by Lt. Colonel M. A. Alexandrakis on his return to Athens”</li></ul>",
