 {
  "id": "stop-33-1-67",
  "name": "1950-08 · American Embassy, Athens",
  "availability": "1950-08-01T00:00:00Z/1950-08-31T23:59:59Z",
  "description": "<h3>Takes his manuscripts to the American Embassy; Ewing introduces him to Willard Allan, who after several meetings asks him 'to work with the Americans'</h3><p>Hristonov and the two Donevs are suggested to him as assistants; he 'established a headquarters and proceeded planning operations to penetrate Bulgaria' (p100). The 1960 account replaces this with Clark/Allen/Ewing as Communists (p139-140).</p><table><tr><th align=left valign=top>Event</th><td>33 · recruitment</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Date</th><td>1950-08 · quality: stated</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Place</th><td>American Embassy, Athens (embassy) · in the file: “Athens” · role: at</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Fix</th><td>37.9838, 23.7275 · APPROXIMATE (google)</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Basis</th><td>self_account</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Names in use</th><td>Diko</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Place note</th><td>1950-51 and 1968 building not established; the present chancery (Vasilissis Sofias 91) dates from 1961. Fix is the city only.</td></tr></table><p><b>Sources</b></p><ul><li>p100 <i>self_account</i> (1953-07-21): “In August 1950 KELLY decided to take his texts to the American Embassy in Athens ... he was asked by Mr. Allan to work with the Americans”</li></ul>",
