 {
  "id": "stop-35-1-73",
  "name": "1950-10 · Lavrion refugee camp",
  "availability": "1950-10-01T00:00:00Z/1950-10-31T23:59:59Z",
  "description": "<h3>Visits Lavrion camp: announces a 'charter and instructions' from Embassy members to form a five-man committee and a 'Democratic Agrarian Bloc'</h3><p>Committee: himself president, Ivan Mitev Hristonov secretary, Ivan Donev Ivanov, Dimiter Donev Ivanov, a fifth unnamed. Tasks: intelligence, underground resistance, sabotage against Bulgaria. Told listeners the committee's HQ location, its two Bulgarian typewriters and its car with US plates (p59, p128).</p><table><tr><th align=left valign=top>Event</th><td>35 · organizing</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Date</th><td>1950-10 · quality: stated</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Place</th><td>Lavrion refugee camp (camp) · in the file: “Lavrion” · role: at</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Fix</th><td>37.7130, 24.0564 · APPROXIMATE (google)</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Basis</th><td>document, summary</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Names in use</th><td>Diko; Lyle O. Kelly</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Place note</th><td>Greek camp for Bulgarian and other refugees, 1947-50s. Fix is the town.</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Event note</th><td>Reported to OSO by a source who called him 'an unprincipled opportunist and Greek agent' (p60).</td></tr></table><p><b>Sources</b></p><ul><li>p58 <i>document</i> (1950-12-14): “Early in October 1950, Subject visited the Lavrion Camp ... given a \"charter and instructions,\" by certain members of the American Embassy, to form a committee of five members”</li><li>p59 <i>document</i> (1950-12-14): “the members of the committee at present were: himself as president; Ivan Mitev Hristonov, secretary; Ivan Donev Ivanov; Dimiter Donev Ivanov”</li><li>p128 <i>summary</i> (1961-12-06): “Early in October, 1950, he visited the Lavrion Camp where he spoke to the Bulgarian refugees and outlined the tasks that he was to assume”</li></ul>",
  "position": {
