 {
  "id": "stop-40-1-73",
  "name": "1950-11-01 · Lavrion refugee camp",
  "availability": "1950-11-01T00:00:00Z/1950-11-01T23:59:59Z",
  "description": "<h3>Second Lavrion visit: recruits divided into intelligence (10), radio-in-Germany (6) and sabotage (15) groups; six of Group A move to Athens c. 10 Nov</h3><p>Group A: Zlatev, Kiryanov, Hristonov, Gogov, Djadiev and one unknown. Radio: Iskrov, Popov, G. Nikolov. Sabotage: Kouyoumdjiev, Manev, Todorov, Korchev (p59).</p><table><tr><th align=left valign=top>Event</th><td>40 · organizing</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Date</th><td>1950-11-01 · quality: stated</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Place</th><td>Lavrion refugee camp (camp) · in the file: “Lavrion” · role: at</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Fix</th><td>37.7130, 24.0564 · APPROXIMATE (google)</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Basis</th><td>document</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Names in use</th><td>Diko; Lyle O. Kelly</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Place note</th><td>Greek camp for Bulgarian and other refugees, 1947-50s. Fix is the town.</td></tr></table><p><b>Sources</b></p><ul><li>p12 <i>document</i>: “1 November 1950: DIMITROV again visited the Lavrion Camp”</li><li>p59 <i>document</i> (1950-12-14): “On 1 November 1950, Subject again visited the Lavrion Camp to inform his recruits that they would shortly be moved to a pleasant home in Athens”</li></ul>",
