 {
  "id": "stop-65-1-43",
  "name": "1951 · Sofia",
  "availability": "1951-01-01T00:00:00Z/1951-12-31T23:59:59Z",
  "description": "<h3>Sofia show trial exposes the infiltration operation; one of Dimitrov's chosen agents 'probably an operative of the Bulgarian Militia and ... the betrayer of his colleagues'</h3><table><tr><th align=left valign=top>Event</th><td>65 · trial</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Date</th><td>1951 · quality: stated</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Place</th><td>Sofia (city) · role: at</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Fix</th><td>42.6977, 23.3219 · APPROXIMATE (google)</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Basis</th><td>summary</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Names in use</th><td>Diko; Lyle O. Kelly; Christo Zutoff (tentative)</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Event note</th><td>The file never names the suspected betrayer; the OSO source's 'dangerous Communist' Kouyoumdjiev (p60) is the only candidate it offers.</td></tr></table><p><b>Sources</b></p><ul><li>p13 <i>summary</i>: “an ill-fated operation which resulted in a major expose and trial in Sofia during 1951”</li><li>p34 <i>summary</i>: “The operation resulted in a major expose and trial in Sofia during 1951”</li><li>p104 <i>summary</i> (1953-03-27): “The operation resulted in a major expose and trial in Sofia during 1951”</li></ul>",
