 {
  "id": "stop-46-2-66",
  "name": "1951-02 · 13 Patissia Street, Athens",
  "availability": "1951-02-01T00:00:00Z/1951-02-28T23:59:59Z",
  "description": "<h3>Three Bloc men arrive from IRO camps; ~$850 rent advance credited to Kelly's account; quarters 'very inadequate, insecure and unhealthy'</h3><p>Cited in Jan 1952 as 'financial finagling'; a further $100+ cash shortage found at his removal (p111).</p><table><tr><th align=left valign=top>Event</th><td>46 · organizing</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Date</th><td>1951-02 · quality: stated</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Place</th><td>13 Patissia Street, Athens (address, now Patision 13) · in the file: “13 Patissia Street” · role: at</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Fix</th><td>37.9850, 23.7293 · RANGE_INTERPOLATED (google)</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Basis</th><td>document</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Names in use</th><td>Diko; Lyle O. Kelly</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Link note</th><td>Offices rented for the Bloc (p84, April 1951); attached here as the quarters of early 1951.</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Place note</th><td>Offices Kelly rented for the Bloc, 1951 (p84).</td></tr></table><p><b>Sources</b></p><ul><li>p111 <i>document</i> (1952-01): “In February, 1951, when Kelly was head of the Bulgarian Democratic Bloc, three of his men arrived in Athens, coming directly from IRO camps”</li></ul>",
