 {
  "id": "stop-47-1-65",
  "name": "1951-03-03 · Athens",
  "availability": "1951-03-03T00:00:00Z/1951-03-03T23:59:59Z",
  "description": "<h3>Signs a receipt for $300 from 'Lawrence F. MacBride, literary agent' for a six-month option on three books</h3><p>The $300 was actually Nasmith's; Kelly told the true author that Nasmith had forced him to sign so as to steal it himself (p84).</p><table><tr><th align=left valign=top>Event</th><td>47 · agreement</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Date</th><td>1951-03-03 · quality: stated</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Place</th><td>Athens (city) · role: at</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Fix</th><td>37.9838, 23.7275 · APPROXIMATE (google)</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Basis</th><td>document</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Names in use</th><td>Diko; Lyle O. Kelly</td></tr></table><p><b>Sources</b></p><ul><li>p17 <i>document</i> (1951-03-03): “DIMITROV signed a memorandum certifying that he had received three hundred dollars from Lawrence F. MacBRIDE, literary agent”</li><li>p84 <i>document</i> (1951-04-18): “On one occasion Nasmith personally gave Kelly $300 in dollars for an option on his books. Kelly signed a receipt for this”</li></ul>",
