 {
  "id": "stop-52-1-65",
  "name": "1951-04-12 · Athens",
  "availability": "1951-04-12T00:00:00Z/1951-04-12T23:59:59Z",
  "description": "<h3>Kelly says Florimond wants an answer by the 13th; OPC tells him the answer is 'a definite, final no' and never to see the French again</h3><p>Kelly had reported the Salonika vice-consul's approach 'in early 1951' and been allowed to keep seeing him until OPC learned what the French wanted (p108, p111).</p><table><tr><th align=left valign=top>Event</th><td>52 · contact</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Date</th><td>1951-04-12 · quality: stated</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Place</th><td>Athens (city) · role: at</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Fix</th><td>37.9838, 23.7275 · APPROXIMATE (google)</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Basis</th><td>document</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Names in use</th><td>Diko; Lyle O. Kelly</td></tr></table><p><b>Sources</b></p><ul><li>p22 <i>document</i> (1951-04-18): “he was to tell FLORIMOND by 13 April whether he would work with him. DIMITROV asked for instructions. He was told that his answer was to be a definte and final no”</li><li>p83 <i>document</i> (1951-04-18): “On Thursday April 12 Kelly stated that he was to tell Florimond by Friday, April 13, whether or not he would work with him”</li></ul>",
  "position": {
