 {
  "id": "stop-55-1-65",
  "name": "1951-04-18 · Athens",
  "availability": "1951-04-18T00:00:00Z/1951-04-18T23:59:59Z",
  "description": "<h3>Picked up by the Greek Aliens Directorate (BGKANTAR) on OPC's order and put under 'protective arrest'; told his life is threatened, 'does not know of our role'</h3><p>Ordered by Henry McLean per p112; Manfield's cable. Kelly's 1953 version: 'apprehended by the Greek Police, allegedly for safe keeping in April 1951' (p101). His 1960 version: arrested at Allen's request near the Soviet Embassy, then four months on a Greek island (p140).</p><table><tr><th align=left valign=top>Event</th><td>55 · pickup</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Date</th><td>1951-04-18 · quality: conflicting</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Place</th><td>Athens (city) · role: at</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Fix</th><td>37.9838, 23.7275 · APPROXIMATE (google)</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Basis</th><td>document, summary, self_account</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Names in use</th><td>Diko; Lyle O. Kelly</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Other dates</th><td>p33 says 1951-04-17; p101 says 1951-04; p140 says 1951</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Event note</th><td>p33 (handwritten chronology) puts the pickup on 17 April alongside the Piray meeting; every contemporary document says 18 April.</td></tr></table><p><b>Sources</b></p><ul><li>p33 <i>summary</i>: “17 April 1951: ... Picked up by Greek Alien Directorate”</li><li>p95 <i>document</i> (1951-04-20): “ON 18 APRIL WE HAD LYLE O. KELLY PICKED UP BY BGKANTAR AND PUT UNDER PROTECTIVE ARREST. HE IS TOLD LIFE IS THREATENED AND DOES NOT KNOW OF OUR ROLE”</li><li>p101 <i>self_account</i> (1953-07-21): “he was apprehended by the Greek Police, allegedly for safe keeping in April 1951”</li><li>p108 <i>summary</i> (1952-02-29): “Arrangements were therefore made with Greek authorities for Kelly's arrest just prior to his scheduled meeting with the French representative”</li><li>p112 <i>document</i> (1952-01): “Kelly was immediately picked up by the Greek Alien Directorate, acting upon orders from Henry McLean”</li><li>p117 <i>document</i> (1951-05-09): “Manfield cabled that he had had the Greek Aliens Directorate pick up Dimitrov and put him under protective arrest”</li><li>p140 <i>self_account</i> (1960-06-28): “That night Dimitroff was called to a building near the Soviet Embassy where he was arrested by Greek police at Allen's request”</li></ul>",
  "position": {
   "cartographicDegrees": [
    23.7275388,
    37.9838096,
