 {
  "id": "stop-66-1-65",
  "name": "1951-09 · Athens (from)",
  "availability": "1951-09-01T00:00:00Z/1951-09-02T00:00:00Z",
  "description": "<h3>Flown from Athens to Frankfurt by CIA plane; four days in hospital 'for observation'; then to Panama by US Army plane</h3><p>'To facilitate his removal, Subject was told that he was being taken to the United States for a meeting of important satellite refugee leaders' (p104). His 1960 version: Allen gave him a passport as 'Christo Zutoff', a week in Frankfurt, six car changes to the airport, the Azores, Bermuda, then Panama (p140). This Frankfurt stop is the file's only overlap with the Gladych/Ecke geography.</p><table><tr><th align=left valign=top>Event</th><td>66 · transfer</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Date</th><td>1951-09 · quality: circa</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Place</th><td>Athens (city) · role: from</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Fix</th><td>37.9838, 23.7275 · APPROXIMATE (google)</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Basis</th><td>summary, self_account</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Names in use</th><td>Diko; Lyle O. Kelly; Christo Zutoff (tentative)</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Other dates</th><td>p35 says 1951-09-05</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Event note</th><td>Handwritten chronology: 'Left Frankfurt for Panama where he arrived on 5 September' (p35), so the Frankfurt stay was c. 31 Aug - 4/5 Sep 1951.</td></tr></table><p><b>Sources</b></p><ul><li>p35 <i>summary</i>: “5 September 1951: Left Frankfurt for Panama”</li><li>p38 <i>summary</i> (1969-08-25): “He was airlifted from Athens to Frankfurt where he was hospitalized four days for observation, and then flown to the holding facility”</li><li>p104 <i>summary</i> (1953-03-27): “He was flown by CIA plane to Germany, and from there to Panama by U.S. Army plane”</li><li>p140 <i>self_account</i> (1960-06-28): “Allen took him on a military plane from Athens to Italy to Frankfurt where they had to remain for documents for about a week”</li></ul>",
  "position": {
