 {
  "id": "stop-67-1-108",
  "name": "1951-09-04 · Fort Clayton",
  "availability": "1951-09-04T00:00:00Z/1951-09-04T23:59:59Z",
  "description": "<h3>Arrives at Fort Clayton, Panama (DTROBALO); placed in hospital detention as a 'neuro-psychiatric case'</h3><p>'Detained for mental observation and treatment' (p57). Kelly thought 'the hospital was an exterminating establishment for undesirables' until 'Mr. Stanley' reassured him (p101). His 1960 account: a cell in a hospital, Dr. Stafford(?), Ivan Stanley from Washington, Sergeant Barry warning of 'a Communist ring' (p140).</p><table><tr><th align=left valign=top>Event</th><td>67 · detention</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Date</th><td>1951-09-04 · quality: conflicting</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Place</th><td>Fort Clayton (base, now Ciudad del Saber (Clayton)) · in the file: “Fort Clayton, Panama” · role: at</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Fix</th><td>9.0014, -79.5814 · APPROXIMATE (google)</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Basis</th><td>summary, self_account</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Names in use</th><td>Diko; Lyle O. Kelly</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Other dates</th><td>p35 says 1951-09-05; p57 says 1951-09; p101 says 1951-09-05; p129 says 1951-09-06</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Place note</th><td>US Army post in the Canal Zone; CIA holding facility DTROBALO/DTRABALO. Kelly held here 4 Sep 1951 - Jan 1954. Since 1999 the Ciudad del Saber campus.</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Event note</th><td>Arrival date: 4 Sep (p38, p134), 5 Sep (p35, p101), 6 Sep (p129).</td></tr></table><p><b>Sources</b></p><ul><li>p35 <i>summary</i>: “He was placed in detention at a hospital in Panama”</li><li>p38 <i>summary</i> (1969-08-25): “flown to the holding facility, arriving on 4 September 1951”</li><li>p57 <i>summary</i> (1964-01-20): “By September 1951, his behavior had become so peculiar that he was detained for mental observation and treatment”</li><li>p101 <i>self_account</i> (1953-07-21): “he was transported to Panama where he arrived on 5 September 1951. He was placed in detention at a hospital in Panama”</li><li>p129 <i>summary</i> (1961-12-06): “Subject was taken to Panama on 6 September 1951 and was considered as a neuro-psychiatric case”</li><li>p134 <i>summary</i> (1960-07-01): “flown black to Fort Clayton, arriving on 4 September 1951”</li></ul>",
  "position": {
