 {
  "id": "stop-69-1-108",
  "name": "1951-10-09 · Fort Clayton",
  "availability": "1951-10-09T00:00:00Z/1951-10-14T23:59:59Z",
  "description": "<h3>Hunger strike from midnight 9 October to 9 a.m. 14 October; asks that his former partisan secretary be brought from Bulgaria</h3><p>'The doctors' concern, particularly the neuro-psychiatrist, indicated that they could not treat Subject adequately' (p129).</p><table><tr><th align=left valign=top>Event</th><td>69 · hunger_strike</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Date</th><td>1951-10-09 → 1951-10-14 · quality: stated</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Place</th><td>Fort Clayton (base, now Ciudad del Saber (Clayton)) · in the file: “Fort Clayton, Panama” · role: at</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Fix</th><td>9.0014, -79.5814 · APPROXIMATE (google)</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Basis</th><td>summary, self_account</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Names in use</th><td>Diko; Lyle O. Kelly</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Place note</th><td>US Army post in the Canal Zone; CIA holding facility DTROBALO/DTRABALO. Kelly held here 4 Sep 1951 - Jan 1954. Since 1999 the Ciudad del Saber campus.</td></tr></table><p><b>Sources</b></p><ul><li>p129 <i>summary</i> (1961-12-06): “On 9 October 1951, he began a hunger strike at midnight and did not break the fast until 9 a.m. on 14 October 1951”</li><li>p140 <i>self_account</i> (1960-06-28): “After a five-day hunger strike”</li></ul>",
