 {
  "id": "stop-76-1-108",
  "name": "1951-12-27 · Fort Clayton (from)",
  "availability": "1951-12-27T00:00:00Z/1951-12-27T23:59:59Z",
  "description": "<h3>Letter to a friend in Greece: 'I succeeded in leaving Greece, and freeing my soul from the slavery of Flora'</h3><table><tr><th align=left valign=top>Event</th><td>76 · correspondence</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Date</th><td>1951-12-27 · quality: stated</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Place</th><td>Fort Clayton (base, now Ciudad del Saber (Clayton)) · in the file: “Panama” · role: from</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Fix</th><td>9.0014, -79.5814 · APPROXIMATE (google)</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Basis</th><td>document</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Names in use</th><td>Diko; Lyle O. Kelly</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Place note</th><td>US Army post in the Canal Zone; CIA holding facility DTROBALO/DTRABALO. Kelly held here 4 Sep 1951 - Jan 1954. Since 1999 the Ciudad del Saber campus.</td></tr></table><p><b>Sources</b></p><ul><li>p113 <i>document</i> (1952-01): “Letter written by Kelly to a friend in Greece, dated 27 December, 1951: ... freeing my soul from the slavery of Flora”</li></ul>",
