 {
  "id": "stop-79-1-108",
  "name": "1952-03 · Fort Clayton",
  "availability": "1952-03-01T00:00:00Z/1952-03-31T23:59:59Z",
  "description": "<h3>Transferred from the Panama hospital to DTROBALO proper</h3><p>Handwritten 'JIROBALO' (p35). Kelly: six months there, then confrontation over release, a threat to walk out, and confinement until May 1953 (p101). 1960 version: 'an old abandoned coast artillery building' at Colon with five civilian guards, later a shell magazine for seven months (p141).</p><table><tr><th align=left valign=top>Event</th><td>79 · transfer</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Date</th><td>1952-03 · quality: stated</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Place</th><td>Fort Clayton (base, now Ciudad del Saber (Clayton)) · in the file: “Fort Clayton, Panama” · role: at</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Fix</th><td>9.0014, -79.5814 · APPROXIMATE (google)</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Basis</th><td>summary, self_account</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Names in use</th><td>Diko; Lyle O. Kelly</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Link note</th><td>Hospital to DTROBALO proper.</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Place note</th><td>US Army post in the Canal Zone; CIA holding facility DTROBALO/DTRABALO. Kelly held here 4 Sep 1951 - Jan 1954. Since 1999 the Ciudad del Saber campus.</td></tr></table><p><b>Sources</b></p><ul><li>p35 <i>summary</i>: “March 1952: Transferred to JIROBALO”</li><li>p101 <i>self_account</i> (1953-07-21): “In March 1952 KELLY was transferred to DTROBALO”</li><li>p141 <i>self_account</i> (1960-06-28): “Actually he was taken to Colon to an old abandoned coast artillery building”</li></ul>",
