  "name": "1952-09 · Fort Clayton",
  "availability": "1952-09-01T00:00:00Z/1953-05-31T23:59:59Z",
  "description": "<h3>After demanding release, threatens to leave; 'apprehended and placed in confinement until his release in May 1953'</h3><p>Hemovich's gloss: 'His confinement at DTROBALO was to prevent his contemplated and announced escape' (p102). 1960 version: tied and gagged at the airport after a promise of Mexico, seven months in a shell magazine (p141).</p><table><tr><th align=left valign=top>Event</th><td>81 · detention</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Date</th><td>1952-09 → 1953-05 · quality: circa</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Place</th><td>Fort Clayton (base, now Ciudad del Saber (Clayton)) · in the file: “Fort Clayton, Panama” · role: at</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Fix</th><td>9.0014, -79.5814 · APPROXIMATE (google)</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Basis</th><td>self_account</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Names in use</th><td>Diko; Lyle O. Kelly</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Place note</th><td>US Army post in the Canal Zone; CIA holding facility DTROBALO/DTRABALO. Kelly held here 4 Sep 1951 - Jan 1954. Since 1999 the Ciudad del Saber campus.</td></tr></table><p><b>Sources</b></p><ul><li>p101 <i>self_account</i> (1953-07-21): “Approximately one month later KELLY said he informed the Station authorities that he would leave the area if they did not release him as initially promised. He stated that he was apprehended and placed in confinement unt…”</li><li>p141 <i>self_account</i> (1960-06-28): “He was tied and gagged in the Communist fashion and taken back by the ambulance to the same artillery area but placed in an old shell magazine under guard”</li></ul>",
