 {
  "id": "stop-85-1-108",
  "name": "1953-05-26 · Fort Clayton",
  "availability": "1953-05-26T00:00:00Z/1953-05-27T23:59:59Z",
  "description": "<h3>Major Hemovich ('Mike Vargas') arrives at DTROBALO; twelve-hour interview with Kelly in Serbo-Croatian on 27 May</h3><p>Kelly 'has been waiting 25 months to speak to someone from Washington'. Verdict: 'KELLY knows little about operations in Greece'; recommend resettlement (p103).</p><table><tr><th align=left valign=top>Event</th><td>85 · interview</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Date</th><td>1953-05-26 → 1953-05-27 · quality: stated</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Place</th><td>Fort Clayton (base, now Ciudad del Saber (Clayton)) · in the file: “Fort Clayton, Panama” · role: at</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Fix</th><td>9.0014, -79.5814 · APPROXIMATE (google)</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Basis</th><td>document, summary</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Names in use</th><td>Diko; Lyle O. Kelly</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Place note</th><td>US Army post in the Canal Zone; CIA holding facility DTROBALO/DTRABALO. Kelly held here 4 Sep 1951 - Jan 1954. Since 1999 the Ciudad del Saber campus.</td></tr></table><p><b>Sources</b></p><ul><li>p45 <i>summary</i> (1967-04-04): “In May 1953, a CIA case officer was dispatched from Headquarters”</li><li>p97 <i>document</i> (1953-07-21): “I flew to DTROBALO, arriving there at noon on 26 May 1953 ... At 0800 hours 27 May KELLY's case officer escorted me to the pre-arranged meeting site and introduced me as Mike Vargas”</li><li>p127 <i>document</i> (1953-07-21): “Major Michael A. Hemovich was sent to DTROBALO where he arrived at noon on 26 May 1953”</li><li>p134 <i>summary</i> (1960-07-01): “A CIA case officer was dispatched from headquarters in May 1953 to Fort Clayton where he interrogated Subject”</li></ul>",
  "position": {
