  "name": "1954-01 · Syros refugee detention camp (to)",
  "availability": "1954-02-28T23:59:59Z/1954-03-01T23:59:59Z",
  "description": "<h3>Holding facility at Fort Clayton terminated; Kelly 'temporarily removed' to Greece; Syros refugee detention camp under Greek custody from February 1954</h3><p>CIA commits to the Greeks not to abandon him and to move him within a year. Efforts to place him in Brazil, Canada, New Zealand and Australia fail (p38, p46, p135). His 1960 version: three men 'from Vice President Nixon's office' rescue him, hotel in Cristobal, returned 'in the Spring of 1954' (p141).</p><table><tr><th align=left valign=top>Event</th><td>90 · transfer</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Date</th><td>1954-01 → 1954-02 · quality: stated</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Place</th><td>Syros refugee detention camp (camp) · in the file: “Syros” · role: to</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Fix</th><td>37.4418, 24.9404 · APPROXIMATE (google)</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Basis</th><td>summary, self_account</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Names in use</th><td>Diko; Lyle O. Kelly</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Other dates</th><td>p57 says 1954-02; p129 says 1954-02; p141 says 1954</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Place note</th><td>Greek custody Feb 1954-1956. Exact site not established; fix is Ermoupoli.</td></tr></table><p><b>Sources</b></p><ul><li>p38 <i>summary</i> (1969-08-25): “He remained there until January 1954 ... After unsuccessful efforts to resettle KELLY in Brazil, he was temporarily removed from the holding area to Syros, Greece”</li><li>p57 <i>summary</i> (1964-01-20): “In February 1954, Subject was considered well enough to be returned to normal refugee channels in Greece and was transferred to the Syros refugee detention camp”</li><li>p129 <i>summary</i> (1961-12-06): “In February, 1954, Subject was returned to Greece”</li><li>p135 <i>summary</i> (1960-07-01): “With termination of the holding facility at Fort Clayton, Subject was temporarily removed to Greece”</li><li>p141 <i>self_account</i> (1960-06-28): “They returned him in the Spring of 1954 to the Greek authorities in Athens”</li></ul>",
