 {
  "id": "stop-89-1-108",
  "name": "1954-01-08 · Fort Clayton",
  "availability": "1954-01-08T00:00:00Z/1954-01-12T23:59:59Z",
  "description": "<h3>Entler visits DTRABALO; Kelly signs the Syros agreement / 'Certificate of Understanding' (o/a 12 Jan 1954)</h3><p>Kelly asks: wife and child at Syros? Greek jurisdiction? 'Is this office throwing him out completely?' Answer: 'This office will always keep a check on anyone who has ever had connections with it.' He wanted to know 'whether the Americans or the Greeks were responsible' for 1951 and 'agreed to forget the matter' (p124). THROWOFF/3 signed reluctantly; GOHAVEN refused (p124-125).</p><table><tr><th align=left valign=top>Event</th><td>89 · agreement</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Date</th><td>1954-01-08 → 1954-01-12 · quality: stated</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Place</th><td>Fort Clayton (base, now Ciudad del Saber (Clayton)) · in the file: “Fort Clayton, Panama” · role: at</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Fix</th><td>9.0014, -79.5814 · APPROXIMATE (google)</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Basis</th><td>document, summary</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Names in use</th><td>Diko; Lyle O. Kelly</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Other dates</th><td>p45 says 1954-01-12; p135 says 1954-01-12</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Place note</th><td>US Army post in the Canal Zone; CIA holding facility DTROBALO/DTRABALO. Kelly held here 4 Sep 1951 - Jan 1954. Since 1999 the Ciudad del Saber campus.</td></tr></table><p><b>Sources</b></p><ul><li>p45 <i>summary</i> (1967-04-04): “On or about 12 January 1954, while still at [REDACTED] the Subject signed a Certificate of Understanding”</li><li>p123 <i>document</i> (1954-01-28): “On 8 January 1954, James P. Entler arrived in DTRABALO to contact Subjects. The primary purpose of the contact was to persuade Subjects to sign the Syros agreement”</li><li>p124 <i>document</i> (1954-01-28): “Kelly was contacted on 8 January and again on 9 January at his request”</li><li>p135 <i>summary</i> (1960-07-01): “The attached understanding with Subject was effected o/a 12 January 1954 at the time of his removal from Fort Clayton”</li></ul>",
