 {
  "id": "stop-91-2-76",
  "name": "1955-10 · Syros refugee detention camp",
  "availability": "1955-10-01T00:00:00Z/1955-10-31T23:59:59Z",
  "description": "<h3>Seeks admission to the United States under the Refugee Relief Program; CIA decides not to object, 'without any assistance from CIA'</h3><p>p119: 'He came to the U. S. with the aid of the Queen of Greece' (State Dept relay of his claim); p141: US immigration official James T. Martin 'assisted his departure'.</p><table><tr><th align=left valign=top>Event</th><td>91 · immigration</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Date</th><td>1955-10 · quality: stated</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Place</th><td>Syros refugee detention camp (camp) · in the file: “Syros” · role: at</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Fix</th><td>37.4418, 24.9404 · APPROXIMATE (google)</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Basis</th><td>summary, self_account</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Names in use</th><td>Diko; Lyle O. Kelly</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Link note</th><td>Where he was held 1954-56.</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Place note</th><td>Greek custody Feb 1954-1956. Exact site not established; fix is Ermoupoli.</td></tr></table><p><b>Sources</b></p><ul><li>p119 <i>self_account</i> (1957-05-14): “He came to the U. S. with the aid of the Queen of Greece”</li><li>p129 <i>summary</i> (1961-12-06): “In October, 1955, Subject sought admission to the United States under the Refugee Relief Program”</li><li>p135 <i>summary</i> (1960-07-01): “let him immigrate to the United States on his own under the Refugee Relief Act program, but without any assistance from CIA”</li></ul>",
