 {
  "id": "stop-96-2-114",
  "name": "1957-05-14 · 2036 P Street NW, Washington",
  "availability": "1957-05-14T00:00:00Z/1957-05-14T23:59:59Z",
  "description": "<h3>State Department tells CIA he is in Washington (2036 P Street tourist home) trying to sell a feature-length script; RQM/OIS source-lead memo to Chief, SR; CIA declines to meet him</h3><p>Lives in Newark with wife and seven-year-old child; 'approximately 32'.</p><table><tr><th align=left valign=top>Event</th><td>96 · memo</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Date</th><td>1957-05-14 · quality: stated</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Place</th><td>2036 P Street NW, Washington (address) · in the file: “2036 P Street tourist home” · role: at</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Fix</th><td>38.9094, -77.0464 · RANGE_INTERPOLATED (google)</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Basis</th><td>document, summary · State tells CIA he is staying at 2036 P Street NW</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Names in use</th><td>Dim. Ad. Dimitroff; Diko; Lyle O. Kelly</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Place note</th><td>Julia Rogers Smith's tourist home; his lodging May 1957 (p119).</td></tr></table><p><b>Sources</b></p><ul><li>p46 <i>summary</i> (1967-04-04): “On 14 May 1957, the Department of State informed CIA that the Subject had contacted their Office”</li><li>p119 <i>document</i> (1957-05-14): “We have been informed by the Department of State that Dimitur Adamov DIMITROV (aka DIKO) is presently in Washington ... for the purpose of interesting any U. S. Government agency in a feature-length film script”</li><li>p135 <i>summary</i> (1960-07-01): “On 14 May 1957, the Department of State informed CIA”</li></ul>",
