 {
  "id": "stop-101-2-135",
  "name": "1958-05-27 · 1424 S. Kenmore Avenue, Los Angeles (to)",
  "availability": "1958-05-27T00:00:00Z/1958-05-27T23:59:59Z",
  "description": "<h3>Cushman, for Vice President Nixon, acknowledges his 20 May letter on 'plans to fight Communism' and steers him to State and USIA</h3><p>Prompted by Nixon's Caracas trip; Dimitrov's 1960 telling (p142).</p><table><tr><th align=left valign=top>Event</th><td>101 · correspondence</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Date</th><td>1958-05-27 · quality: stated</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Place</th><td>1424 S. Kenmore Avenue, Los Angeles (address) · in the file: “Los Angeles” · role: to</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Fix</th><td>34.0458, -118.2967 · RANGE_INTERPOLATED (google)</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Basis</th><td>document, self_account</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Names in use</th><td>Dim. Ad. Dimitroff; Diko; Lyle O. Kelly</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Place note</th><td>His address, May 1958 (p144, p145).</td></tr></table><p><b>Sources</b></p><ul><li>p142 <i>self_account</i> (1960-06-28): “Dimitroff wrote to President Eisenhower again, receiving an answer from Cushman of the Vice President's office”</li><li>p144 <i>document</i> (1958-05-27): “On behalf of the Vice President I wish to acknowledge your letter of May 20 concerning your plans to fight Communism”</li></ul>",
