 {
  "id": "stop-103-2-115",
  "name": "1960-06-27 · Lettermen's Tourist Home, 2939 F Street NW, Washington",
  "availability": "1960-06-27T00:00:00Z/1960-06-28T23:59:59Z",
  "description": "<h3>'Dimitre Cutzupolous' asks Nixon's office for an appointment; Cushman has Contact Division call him; Sheridan interviews 'Dim. Ad. Dimitroff' for a full day on 28 June</h3><p>Asks to be Nixon's anti-Communist adviser for the Balkans; wants $10-12,000 to finish a 400-500 page book that would help Nixon win; tells the full 1943-1956 story with Allen and Ewing as Communists and Nixon's men as his Panama rescuers; registered at his tourist home as 'Gatzoyolous'. 'Believes that in talking to Sheridan he was talking to a member of Mr. Nixon's staff' (p142).</p><table><tr><th align=left valign=top>Event</th><td>103 · interview</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Date</th><td>1960-06-27 → 1960-06-28 · quality: stated</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Place</th><td>Lettermen's Tourist Home, 2939 F Street NW, Washington (address) · in the file: “Lettermen's Tourist Home, 2939 F Street, N.W.” · role: at</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Fix</th><td>38.8974, -77.0556 · RANGE_INTERPOLATED (google)</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Basis</th><td>document, summary</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Names in use</th><td>Dim. Ad. Dimitroff; Diko; Lyle O. Kelly; Dimitre Cutzupolous</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Link note</th><td>Where he was staying.</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Place note</th><td>His hotel during the June 1960 interviews (p142). Check the interpolated fix: the street number may be an OCR reading.</td></tr></table><p><b>Sources</b></p><ul><li>p46 <i>summary</i> (1967-04-04): “On 28 June 1960, the Subject attempted to arrange a meeting with the then Vice-President Richard M. Nixon”</li><li>p132 <i>summary</i> (1961-10-12): “Dimitroff had been interviewed at length in the Washington Field Office on 28 June 1960”</li><li>p137 <i>document</i> (1960-06-28): “On 27 June, George Forrest notified Sheridan that General Cushman of Vice President Nixon's office had requested an immediate contact with a Dimitre Cutzupolous”</li><li>p143 <i>document</i> (1960-06-28): “F. J. Sheridan / W-13941”</li></ul>",
