  "description": "<h3>Letter to President Kennedy offering to liberate Bulgaria; referred to State, then to CIA</h3><table><tr><th align=left valign=top>Event</th><td>105 · correspondence</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Date</th><td>1961-06-15 · quality: stated</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Place</th><td>Los Angeles (city) · role: from</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Fix</th><td>34.0549, -118.2426 · APPROXIMATE (google)</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Basis</th><td>document, summary</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Names in use</th><td>Diko; Lyle O. Kelly</td></tr></table><p><b>Sources</b></p><ul><li>p38 <i>summary</i> (1969-08-25): “the statement in his letter to President Kennedy that he could liberate the Balkan countries from Communism in five years”</li><li>p133 <i>document</i> (1961-10-12): “To these ends he wrote a letter on 15 June 1961 to President Kennedy (copy attached)”</li></ul>",
