 {
  "id": "stop-107-1-109",
  "name": "1961-10-02 · Washington, D.C.",
  "availability": "1961-10-02T00:00:00Z/1961-10-02T23:59:59Z",
  "description": "<h3>Second Sheridan interview: proposes a 5,000-man airdrop into southern Bulgaria in April 1962 and a 'Liberation Committee'; threatens to name the Americans who held him; script 'One Dark Night'</h3><p>Says Dr. G. M. Dimitrov 'is on the United States payroll and had called him a traitor'. Letter drop as 'Dimitriou' (422 Washington Building) and 'Dimo Petroff' (Toronto).</p><table><tr><th align=left valign=top>Event</th><td>107 · interview</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Date</th><td>1961-10-02 · quality: stated</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Place</th><td>Washington, D.C. (city) · in the file: “Contact Division Washington Office” · role: at</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Fix</th><td>38.9073, -77.0369 · APPROXIMATE (google)</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Basis</th><td>document</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Names in use</th><td>Diko; Lyle O. Kelly; Dimitriou; Dimo Petroff</td></tr></table><p><b>Sources</b></p><ul><li>p132 <i>document</i> (1961-10-12): “an appointment was made for 2 October 1961 at the Washington Field Office”</li><li>p133 <i>document</i> (1961-10-12): “These would be used to invade Bulgaria by air drop into the southern mountain tier about April 1962”</li></ul>",
