 {
  "id": "stop-125-1-117",
  "name": "1964-03-24 · New York City",
  "availability": "1964-03-24T00:00:00Z/1964-03-24T23:59:59Z",
  "description": "<h3>The Film Daily: 'Greek Gods to Roll in '65 at $20 Million Budget'; Diko Productions, 'a new American-Greek company headquartered in Athens', to film in Greece and at Bronston Studios, Madrid</h3><p>Financing 'obtained from Wall Street firm National Organization to Assist Small Business'; four-hour widescreen production, a year's shooting, exteriors on Mount Olympus, start 'next January'. The copy in the file is annotated by hand 'THIS IS WHAT I AM TRYING TO DO NOW' (p54-55), which suggests he sent it in himself. The same 'movie concerning the history of Greek mythology' is what he asked CIA for $50,000 to make in March 1967 (p45).</p><table><tr><th align=left valign=top>Event</th><td>125 · publication</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Date</th><td>1964-03-24 · quality: stated</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Place</th><td>New York City (city) · in the file: “New York” · role: at</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Fix</th><td>40.7128, -74.0060 · APPROXIMATE (google)</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Basis</th><td>document · Film Daily: Diko Productions Inc., New York, Mar 1964</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Names in use</th><td>Diko; Lyle O. Kelly; Diko Dimitroff</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Link note</th><td>Place of publication.</td></tr></table><p><b>Sources</b></p><ul><li>p54 <i>document</i> (1964-03-24): “Diko Prod., Inc., new American-Greek company headquartered in Athens, plans to produce 'The Loves of the Greek Gods' in Greece and at Bronston Studios in Madrid”</li><li>p55 <i>document</i> (1964-03-24): “handwritten_annotation: THIS IS WHAT I AM TRYING TO DO NOW”</li><li>p56 <i>document</i> (1964-03-24): “Diko Dimitroff, head of new company, set next January for start of filming; financing obtained from Wall Street firm National Organization to Assist Small Business”</li></ul>",
  "position": {
   "cartographicDegrees": [
