 {
  "id": "stop-126-1-90",
  "name": "1965-01-22 · Madrid",
  "availability": "1965-01-22T00:00:00Z/1965-01-22T23:59:59Z",
  "description": "<h3>Guidepost (Madrid): 'Diko Dimitroff, Bulgarian-born poet, screen-writer, director and producer' describes his '15-year-old dream' The Loves of the Greek Gods, to shoot from June in Spain and Greece</h3><p>Head of Diko Productions Inc.; interiors in Madrid 'with the use of the Bronston equipment', exteriors on Olympus; wish-list cast Mature, Douglas, Curtis, Ustinov, Simmons; 30,000 extras at Olympia, 65 starring roles, four hours, twenty million dollars. Places him in Madrid in January 1965, which fits the Madrid Embassy liaison's 1965 source report on 'Diko DIMITROFF ... film producer' (p40).</p><table><tr><th align=left valign=top>Event</th><td>126 · interview</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Date</th><td>1965-01-22 · quality: stated</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Place</th><td>Madrid (city) · role: at</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Fix</th><td>40.4167, -3.7033 · APPROXIMATE (google)</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Basis</th><td>document</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Names in use</th><td>Diko; Lyle O. Kelly; Diko Dimitroff</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Other dates</th><td>p40 says 1965</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Place note</th><td>His office, 1965.</td></tr></table><p><b>Sources</b></p><ul><li>p40 <i>document</i> (1969-07-24): “A source of unknown reliability reported in 1965 that Diko DIMITROFF had connections with the Bulgarian Intelligence Service ... DIMITROFF represents himself as a film producer”</li><li>p52 <i>document</i> (1965-01-22): “Going big all the way is Diko Dimitroff, Bulgarian-born poet, screen-writer, director and producer, who flashed into our office this week with plans to make the biggest movie of all time”</li><li>p53 <i>document</i> (1965-01-22): “«I'm using the largest cast ever,» Dimitroff told us, «at Olympia alone there will be 30,000 extras and there are 65 starring roles.»”</li></ul>",
  "position": {
