  "name": "1965-08 · New York City",
  "availability": "1965-08-01T00:00:00Z/1965-08-31T23:59:59Z",
  "description": "<h3>Motion Picture Daily (4 Aug 1965): Pinky Herman lunches with Diko Dimitroff; after two months in New York he leaves for his Madrid office; the Greek-gods epic now 'skedded to start in the Spring of 1966' with 30 international stars</h3><p>Herman likens him to Joseph E. Levine. Third and last dated trace of the film project in the file; in March 1967 he was still seeking money for it (p45).</p><table><tr><th align=left valign=top>Event</th><td>127 · interview</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Date</th><td>1965-08 · quality: stated</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Place</th><td>New York City (city) · in the file: “New York” · role: at</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Fix</th><td>40.7128, -74.0060 · APPROXIMATE (google)</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Basis</th><td>document</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Names in use</th><td>Diko; Lyle O. Kelly; Diko Dimitroff</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Link note</th><td>Two months in New York.</td></tr></table><p><b>Sources</b></p><ul><li>p51 <i>document</i> (1965-08-04): “After two months in Gotham, finalizing pre-production plans, Diko leaves Thursday for his office in Madrid where he'll set in motion his ambitious production on this epic to be filmed in Greece skedded to start in the Sp…”</li></ul>",
