 {
  "id": "stop-116-1-109",
  "name": "1967-03-30 · Washington, D.C.",
  "availability": "1967-03-30T00:00:00Z/1967-03-31T23:59:59Z",
  "description": "<h3>Calls the DCI's office as 'General Dimitrov'; two Office of Security men interview him in his Washington hotel room; congratulates Helms, wants $50,000 for a Greek-mythology film and a 'World Tribunal' against Bertrand Russell</h3><p>Vice-President of the Anti-Communist International. Called back 31 March and told 'if any interest developed he would be contacted' (p47).</p><table><tr><th align=left valign=top>Event</th><td>116 · interview</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Date</th><td>1967-03-30 → 1967-03-31 · quality: stated</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Place</th><td>Washington, D.C. (city) · in the file: “Washington” · role: at</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Fix</th><td>38.9073, -77.0369 · APPROXIMATE (google)</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Basis</th><td>document</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Names in use</th><td>Diko; Dico; General Dico Dimitrov; General Dico Dimitroff; Lyle O. Kelly</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Link note</th><td>Hotel not named.</td></tr></table><p><b>Sources</b></p><ul><li>p44 <i>document</i> (1967-04-04): “On 30 March 1967 the Subject, who identified himself as General Dimitrov, called your Office seeking an interview”</li><li>p45 <i>document</i> (1967-04-04): “to seek $50,000 from CIA to enable him to start production in Greece and Spain on a movie concerning the history of Greek mythology”</li><li>p47 <i>document</i> (1967-04-03): “On 31 March 1967 ... a representative of my Office called the Subject at his hotel”</li></ul>",
