 {
  "id": "stop-117-1-116",
  "name": "1967-03-31 · Astoria Restaurant, Washington",
  "availability": "1967-03-31T00:00:00Z/1967-03-31T23:59:59Z",
  "description": "<h3>Dinner at the Astoria Restaurant with an FI/SIG/SSB officer whose mother he knows; says he has 'seen my boss ... Dick Helms' that Thursday; 'the most rabid anti-communist I have ever met'</h3><p>The officer's mother saw him again 3 April in New York; officer asks guidance because Dimitrov had worked out where he was employed (p43).</p><table><tr><th align=left valign=top>Event</th><td>117 · meeting</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Date</th><td>1967-03-31 · quality: stated</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Place</th><td>Astoria Restaurant, Washington (hotel) · in the file: “Astoria Restaurant” · role: at</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Fix</th><td>38.9073, -77.0369 · MANUAL (manual)</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Basis</th><td>document</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Names in use</th><td>Diko; Dico; General Dico Dimitrov; General Dico Dimitroff; Lyle O. Kelly</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Place note</th><td>Dinner, 31 Mar 1967 (p42). Web lookup 2026-09-23 found no 1960s restaurant of this name; not located. Fixed 2026-09-23 to the Washington city centroid at the researcher's request.</td></tr></table><p><b>Sources</b></p><ul><li>p42 <i>document</i> (1967-05-10): “During the course of the evening, Dico said he had seen my boss. When I asked whom he meant, he replied, Dick Helms”</li><li>p43 <i>document</i> (1967-05-10): “My mother saw him one time (3 April) just after his return to New York”</li></ul>",
  "position": {
   "cartographicDegrees": [
