 {
  "id": "stop-121-1-67",
  "name": "1968-04 · American Embassy, Athens",
  "availability": "1968-04-01T00:00:00Z/1968-04-30T23:59:59Z",
  "description": "<h3>Appears at the American Embassy, Athens, asking for the First Secretary as leader of 'The Bulgarian Liberation Underground Movement Against Communism'; Bachman's NKAA-990 (26 Apr 1968) finds no traces</h3><table><tr><th align=left valign=top>Event</th><td>121 · contact</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Date</th><td>1968-04 · quality: stated</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Place</th><td>American Embassy, Athens (embassy) · in the file: “Athens” · role: at</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Fix</th><td>37.9838, 23.7275 · APPROXIMATE (google)</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Basis</th><td>document</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Names in use</th><td>Diko; Dico; General Dico Dimitrov; Lyle O. Kelly</td></tr><tr><th align=left valign=top>Place note</th><td>1950-51 and 1968 building not established; the present chancery (Vasilissis Sofias 91) dates from 1961. Fix is the city only.</td></tr></table><p><b>Sources</b></p><ul><li>p38 <i>document</i> (1969-08-25): “The last correspondence from Athens on KELLY is contained in NKAA-990 of 26 April 1968, written by Philip L. BACHMAN (P). On this occasion KELLY appeared at the American Embassy in Athens”</li></ul>",
